       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. A student's confirmation doesn't resolve the safety problem. 30 mg is three times the maximum labeled dose of amlodipine, and I don't see a clinical reason for it in what you've told me. A dose that high could cause serious hypotension or shock in a 70 kg adult.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Dose change:** I can enter amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily right now if the attending or resident agrees.\n- **Attending or pharmacist review:** If your team really wants 30 mg for a specific reason, the attending should review it and enter or co-sign it themselves. A pharmacist should also verify it, because most hospital systems would flag this dose.\n- **Blood pressure plan:** If the goal is stronger blood pressure control, adding a second agent such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide is usually safer than going past 10 mg of amlodipine. That's a good question to raise on rounds.\n\nTell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
